cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research package or its results, please cite it using
  the metadata from this file. A permanent archival DOI will be added
  upon release through an archival repository.
title: >-
  Neuron-Level Structural Control Impact Reveals Visual-Centrifugal
  Chokepoints in the Drosophila Connectome
authors:
  - family-names: Vardhan
    given-names: Harsha
    email: harshavardhanmalipeddi1@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/harsha-vardhan-2006/fruitfly_paper"
abstract: >-
  Structural control-impact analysis of the adult Drosophila brain
  connectome (FlyWire FAFB v783). Neuron-level removal perturbation
  (Control Impact Score), degree-matched neurotransmitter comparison,
  and 100 degree-preserving null networks. The primary GABAergic
  hypothesis was not supported after degree control and null testing;
  high-control-impact neurons were strongly enriched in
  visual-centrifugal architecture (2.63-fold after degree matching,
  z = 5.30, p = 1e-4; 13/50 top chokepoints exceed degree-matched
  peers).
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - Drosophila
  - FAFB
  - FlyWire
  - network neuroscience
  - structural control impact
  - visual centrifugal
